      "math_academy_id": "q-129211",
      "sequence_position": 3,
      "problem": "What is the sum of the leading entries of the $1$st and $3$rd rows in the matrix $A,$ given below?\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 4 & 0 & -3 \\\\ 8 & 5 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -8 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 2 & 1\\end{aligned}]\n$$",
      "worked_solution": "The first non-zero entry of each row (from left to right) is the leading entry. \n\nTherefore, the leading entries of the $1$st and $3$rd rows of  $A$ are $4$ and $-8$, respectively.\n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 4 & 0 & -3 \\\\ 8 & 5 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -8 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 2 & 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nSo, the answer is $4+(-8)=-4.$",
